ment standards laboratory in the united states Headquartered in Gaithersburg. Founded 1901.", "newValue": "The National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST), established in 1901 and headquartered in Gaithersburg, Maryland, serves as the United States' premier measurement standards laboratory. Its inception was driven by the burgeoning needs of the industrial sector in the United States, where the lack of standardized measurements was impeding technological advancement and trade. NIST has played a pivotal role in advancing measurement science, developing standards that underpin a wide range of industries from manufacturing to telecommunications, thus ensuring quality and safety in products and services.

